# Wire Length Calculator

R = float(input("Enter Resistance (ohms): "))
A = float(input("Enter Cross-sectional Area (mm²): "))
rho = float(input("Enter Resistivity (ohm-mm²/m): "))

length = (R * A) / rho

print("Wire Length =", length, "meters")


Example

For:

Resistance = 2 Ω
Area = 1 mm²
Copper resistivity ≈ 0.0175 Ω·mm²/m

Output:

Wire Length ≈ 114.29 meters
